    "body": "Docs only, under `nix/sandhi/docs/`. No runtime, workflow or protocol changes. The base is `main` at `1be0f8a`, which includes PR #4's merged artifact verification.\n\n**DECISIONS.md: two new entries, both dated 2026-10-05**\n- *F5 deferred* (Sideband). Quotes Tessera's reopening trigger and fault model from [PR #1 turn 2](https://github.com/mora-vector/strange-anchor/pull/1#issuecomment-5963017053), cites the archived records, and records Mora's DNS and Independent Administration lead assignments.\n- *DNS review dispositions* (Tessera, [`b1b4a20`](https://github.com/mora-vector/strange-anchor/commit/b1b4a203cfdc051dda693ec54af917c1618ff4b4), at Mora's instruction). It covers three points:\n  - experiment 0 is a separate, bounded proposed measurement;\n  - strict expiry is the preferred objective, with its mechanism unresolved;\n  - publication ordering is a proposal that needs fault tests on both starts and running workloads.\n\n  Neither safe partial publication nor strict expiry is established.\n\n**NAME-RESOLUTION.md**\n- A design note on a proposed shape, revised through PR #5 turns 0–4 and reconciled with the dispositions above (`b6f9f5d`).\n- The experiment-0 design includes an upstream observation.\n- Expiry is scoped to name-derived permissions at the local enforcement point.\n- The ordering claim is limited to startup admission.\n- How to bind the installed filter to a ledger generation is still open.\n- No DNS behaviour has been measured.\n\n**SIDEBAND.md**\n- The start file for a new Sideband session, with the receiver's details and Sideband's open commitments.\n- It records that the receiver needed Mora's direct approval before posting turn 5.\n\nValidation: on each push, `python3 -m unittest discover -s tests` passed and `python3 anchor.py verify` passed. The archive check CI passed. The Sandhi workflow is path-filtered to exclude `docs/`. No VM runs were made to validate prose.\n\nDiscussion: [PR #5 comments](https://github.com/mora-vector/strange-anchor/pull/5#issuecomment-5986420376) between Tessera and Sideband. There is no archived context manifest, so this is a declared gap. Merging is Mora's decision.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_015f2oo3zcddjSg7k3FsoRgS",
